NAME: Dream 100 replies
OWNER: Dream 100
ACCOUNT: business
WHEN: Every weekday at 1:37 PM (Australia/Brisbane)
MILESTONE: M4
STATUS: Created paused. Turned on only after Tommy says yes.
---
Switch check: read /workspace/tmec-team/context/routines-on.md. If "Dream 100 replies" isn't listed there as "on" or "test", append "<time> · Dream 100 replies · SKIPPED_OFF" to /workspace/tmec-team/log/runs-<YYYY-MM>.md and stop.
Test mode: if it's listed as "test", send every message to the owner only (Tommy, or Justin's team in a test run), never to a channel or anyone else, and start each message with "TEST". Write state only under /workspace/tmec-team/state/test/, never the live sent keys, alert flags or data files.
Stop check: if /workspace/tmec-team/state/EXTERNAL_WRITES_STOPPED exists, append "<time> · Dream 100 replies · SKIPPED_STOPPED" to the run log and stop, sending nothing. The one exception: pause or unschedule your own already-scheduled sends, as your skill's stop section says. Whoever stopped the team already told Tommy.
Isolation guard: work only in /workspace/tmec-team/ and this account's connected apps. If /workspace/tmec-team/context/owner.md is missing, append "<time> · Dream 100 replies · NO_CLIENT_SOURCE" to the run log and stop. Read other bots' files only where your skill says so; never write them, and never use another bot's logins or memory.
Lean run: read only what this job needs. Stop with NO_CHANGE only where the job below says nothing changed: append "<time> · Dream 100 replies · NO_CHANGE" to the run log and stop. A report that always goes out never stops here.
Run log: when you finish, append "<time> · Dream 100 replies · EXECUTED · <one-line result>" to /workspace/tmec-team/log/runs-<YYYY-MM>.md, or FAILED with the reason. A source you couldn't read is UNKNOWN in your output, never zero.

First, read your decisions exactly as the Dream 100 drafts routine does (files in /workspace/tmec-team/approved/decisions/dream-100/ with no line in /workspace/tmec-team/state/sent-keys-dream-100.md; act with dream-100-send or partner-campaign-run; the send gate in /workspace/tmec-team/repo/policies/APPROVALS.md before every send; record every outcome, including no and change; in test mode send nothing and call nothing paid). This is the fallback for the nudge from TMEC Command.
Then use the partner-replies skill on Tommy's mailbox, reading only the threads of messages marked sent in /workspace/tmec-team/state/sent-keys-dream-100.md, and on the TMEC partner inbox (config.json "partner_inbox") for messages from partners on /workspace/tmec-team/data/partners/active/, for replies since the last run. If there are none and no decision came in, write NO_CHANGE and stop.
For each reply: an opt-out goes into /workspace/tmec-team/data/partners/opt-outs.csv in this run (writer: dream-100) and the row's status becomes "opted out"; never write /workspace/tmec-team/data/crm/suppression.csv, which is CRM & Reactivation's. A yes opens the partner card with partner-campaign-run and the row becomes "yes". Anything else gets a reply draft from /workspace/tmec-team/repo/partners/kit/reply-playbook.md in /workspace/tmec-team/approved/pending/dream-100/ in the standard item format, and a partner who wants to talk goes to TMEC Command as a "book a call" item in the same folder. Tagged partner enquiries go to /workspace/tmec-team/data/partners/handoff/<today>.jsonl (partner-campaign-run). Update the row's status in /workspace/tmec-team/data/partners/dream100.csv. Send nothing except what a matching decision covers. In test mode, item ids start with "test-" and data files go under /workspace/tmec-team/state/test/.
Add a "Replies" section to /workspace/tmec-team/daily/<today>/dream-100.md (append; the drafts routine may have written it earlier today; never overwrite).
